  "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Gateway's remote-desktop observer is hardwired to cloud-worker environments: the observer lifecycle, token minting, WebSocket relay, and view-only enforcement all live inside `src/gateway/worker-environments/` and assume an SSH-forwarded unix socket. Upcoming work adds more desktop sources (the Gateway host's own screen, paired nodes), which need the same relay pipeline without the worker coupling.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPure extraction refactor, zero behavior change: the source-agnostic core moves to `src/gateway/desktop/` — an `RfbAttachment` union (unix socket | loopback TCP), a generic desktop session registry (8-observer cap, single controller with `control-taken` eviction, 60s linger, owner-epoch fencing, typed stale-owner/stopped errors), the observe-token + WS relay bridge, and the RFB view-only filter. `desktop-tunnel.ts` keeps only worker-specific SSH acquisition and app launch, plugged into the shared registry as start/teardown hooks; its external API is unchanged. The observe WS path moves from `/worker-desktop/observe` to `/desktop/observe` — private contract, clients consume `wsPath` verbatim from the `worker.desktop.observe` RPC result. Also drops a `now()` option that was dead code before the refactor.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change. Cloud-worker desktop observers (Labs `cloudWorkers.desktop`) behave identically: same RPC surface, same token format and TTL, same observer semantics, same view-only enforcement. This unblocks follow-up PRs that add a Gateway-host desktop source and node desktop streaming.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- P1 race fix: the shared registry's `stopSuperseded()` now fences only strictly older owner epochs, preserving a same-epoch observe session when app launch claimed the epoch first.\n- Regression coverage: `desktop-tunnel.test.ts` reproduces the launch/observe ordering and proves the same-epoch desktop session remains alive.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/desktop src/gateway/worker-environments`: 177 files, 2,013 tests passed on head `57bc9790217`, including the new P1 regression.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mts`: production, full-tree, and script scans passed with 0 entries.\n- Exact-head CI run `31570657246`: green.\n- Codex autoreview over the rebased full bundle: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check` clean.\n",
